## Import deviations

**None.** No import specifier was changed — all three copies are byte-identical
to the canonical sources (verified by `cmp` and by `tests/ui-parity.test.ts`).

## Recorded deviation: compile-graph exclusion (NOT a content deviation)

`ui/panel-model.ts` is the unadapted control-panel template and imports a
layout this extension does not have:

```
ui/panel-model.ts(1,36): error TS2307: Cannot find module '../config.ts'
ui/panel-model.ts(2,10): error TS2305: Module '"../application.ts"' has no exported member 'ExtensionController'
ui/panel-model.ts(2,31): error TS2305: Module '"../application.ts"' has no exported member 'formatSize'
ui/panel-model.ts(3,33): error TS2307: Cannot find module '../metadata.ts'
```

Chosen fix (keeps byte-identity): `tsconfig.json` excludes `ui/panel-model.ts`
from the compile graph until **slice 1** replaces it with the model-discovery
panel model (`dashboardSnapshot` over `buildHomeSummary`/`buildHomeItems`).
Nothing imports the file yet, so behavior is unchanged and byte-identity — not
typechecking — is the active guard. The rejected alternative (rewriting the
import specifiers) would have required fabricating `config.ts` / `metadata.ts`
and an `ExtensionController` with delegate-shaped `enabled` / `mode` /
`itemLimit` / `thresholdBytes` settings that model-discovery does not have.

`ui/settings-panel.ts` and `ui/format.ts` typecheck normally (external
peer-deps and zero imports respectively).
